M4.22 root Git ownership probe diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-28

Error image
-----------
The comprehensive read-only server probe invoked Git for the canonical Control
and application checkouts as `root`. Git rejected those repository reads with
its `dubious ownership` protection because both checkouts belong to `chatops`.

Cause
-----
The probe correctly used root for protected PostgreSQL and system inventory,
but did not switch only its Git subcommands back to the repository owner.
Consequently, the Git fields from that root invocation are empty and are not
accepted as evidence. All remaining inventory output is read-only and valid.

Risk
----
None to either repository or the server. No safe-directory exception was
created, no Git configuration was changed and no file was modified.

Rollback
--------
No server rollback is required because the operation was read-only. This
diagnosis can be reverted with the M4.22 branch.

Approved continuation
---------------------
Repeat only the Git identity, cleanliness and remote checks under `chatops`,
and bind M4.22 evidence exclusively to those successful results.
